CM_ BO_ 1700 "Clarity mode-switch EPS builds (rwd-xray lab/clarity/CLARITY_MODESW_MM_P2): calibration status, 50 Hz. Layout v2 (build 0x02): bytes 2-6 reserved, 0. Layout v3 (angle builds 0x04 = modes 0-3, 0x05 = modes 0-4, rwd-xray lab/clarity/CLARITY_ANGLE_MODE_*): byte 0 bit 3 and bytes 2-6 carry the angle loop. Absent on stock, CleanPTM and P1.";
CM_ SG_ 1700 BUILD_ID "EPS build; implies the frame layout and the modes built in";
CM_ SG_ 1700 ACTIVE_MODE "calibration mode in the EPS RAM now (0 = stock); changes only at LKAS idle";
CM_ SG_ 1700 ANGLE_LOOP_RUNNING "v3: the angle loop is running (mode 3 or 4, request + angle payload + control type angle)";
CM_ SG_ 1700 ANGLE_FAULT "v3: angle-loop fault, output 0, latched until the request drops";
CM_ SG_ 1700 ANGLE_FAULT_WHY "v3: last fault reason: 1 target jump rejected 3 times, 2 stale 0xE4 (> 32 ms), 3 angle sensor invalid";
CM_ SG_ 1700 ANGLE_TARGET_HELD "v3: an accepted target is held";
CM_ SG_ 1700 ANGLE_LOOP_ACTIVE "v3: same as ANGLE_LOOP_RUNNING";
CM_ SG_ 1700 ANGLE_REF "v3: the loop reference angle (filtered, rate-limited target), same scale and sign as STEER_ANGLE";
CM_ SG_ 1700 ANGLE_OUT "v3: the value the loop wrote into the 0xE4 torque latch (STEER_TORQUE units)";
CM_ SG_ 1700 REQUESTED_MODE "(last valid 0xE4 byte 3 >> 1) & 7, 0 if no valid latch";
CM_ BO_ 1700 "Clarity mode-switch EPS builds (rwd-xray lab/clarity/CLARITY_MODESW_MM_P2): calibration status, 50 Hz. Layout v2 (build 0x02): bytes 2-6 reserved, 0. Layout v3 (angle builds 0x04 = modes 0-3, 0x05 = modes 0-4, rwd-xray lab/clarity/CLARITY_ANGLE_MODE_*): byte 0 bit 3 and bytes 2-6 carry the angle loop. Absent on stock, CleanPTM and P1.";
CM_ SG_ 1700 BUILD_ID "EPS build; implies the frame layout and the modes built in";
CM_ SG_ 1700 ACTIVE_MODE "calibration mode in the EPS RAM now (0 = stock); changes only at LKAS idle";
CM_ SG_ 1700 ANGLE_LOOP_RUNNING "v3: the angle loop is running (mode 3 or 4, request + angle payload + control type angle)";
CM_ SG_ 1700 ANGLE_FAULT "v3: angle-loop fault, output 0, latched until the request drops";
CM_ SG_ 1700 ANGLE_FAULT_WHY "v3: last fault reason: 1 target jump rejected 3 times, 2 stale 0xE4 (> 32 ms), 3 angle sensor invalid";
CM_ SG_ 1700 ANGLE_TARGET_HELD "v3: an accepted target is held";
CM_ SG_ 1700 ANGLE_LOOP_ACTIVE "v3: same as ANGLE_LOOP_RUNNING";
CM_ SG_ 1700 ANGLE_REF "v3: the loop reference angle (filtered, rate-limited target), same scale and sign as STEER_ANGLE";
CM_ SG_ 1700 ANGLE_OUT "v3: the value the loop wrote into the 0xE4 torque latch (STEER_TORQUE units)";
CM_ SG_ 1700 REQUESTED_MODE "(last valid 0xE4 byte 3 >> 1) & 7, 0 if no valid latch";
